  "notes": "Closed-score SATB: Soprano+Alto share the treble staff, Tenor+Bass share the bass staff. A correct conversion yields FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), each with its own notes; all three verses belong to the Soprano part (lyric numbers 1-3) and must stay attached to soprano notes, including melisma skips (e.g. \"pre - cious\" spans a slurred melisma). DAMAGE (combo): Everything at once. mild: aged paper, bleed-through, a few pencil marks, 3 deg skew, JPEG 60. scan: phone photo (250 dpi) of an aged, stained, pencil-marked page with hand shadow, JPEG 50. severe: 150 dpi book scan with curl + gutter, -7 deg skew, foxing, 25% bleed-through, stain, pencil + ballpoint marks, punch holes, motion blur, noise and JPEG 25 - a worst case. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Handwritten marks, stains, foxing and ghost notes are not music and are not in the truth. Severe is intentionally at (or beyond) the limit of human legibility at 150 dpi."
